<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccc} {9}{x}\amp+\amp{8}{y}\amp-\amp{5}{z}\amp-\amp{67}{w}\amp=\amp{43}\\-{4}{x}\amp-\amp{2}{y}\amp+\amp{2}{z}\amp+\amp{20}{w}\amp=\amp-{28}\\{6}{x}\amp+\amp{5}{y}\amp-\amp{6}{z}\amp-\amp{67}{w}\amp=\amp{55}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{6}-{2}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{7}+{5}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{9}-{9}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

